flex type: Directional Flex (increases pop in tail while having stiffer nose for control in all conditions)
shape: Tapered Directional (tail narrower than nose for enhanced control and flotation in deeper snow)
camber type: Directional Camber (rocker in nose for extra float in powder, traditional camber for response and stability)
width options: Standard
mounting system: The Channel (Burton Channel system, compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
laminate: 45° Carbon Highlights (tip to tail carbon layer reduces weight, 45° angled fibres fine tune torsional flex for aggressive ride)
core: Super Fly II 700G Core (stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas for pop and strength while reducing weight)
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker more powerful sections combined with thinner more flexible sections profiled throughout core for enhanced energy transfer)
base: Sintered WFO (Wide F!#@ing Open - extra absorbent high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax)
freeride geometry: Balanced Freeride Geometry (setback camber and stance-centred sidecut, feels like twin when riding flat based but tight turns and effortless float of directional board)
durability technology: Infinite Ride (boards overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery, rides consistently from day one to day 100)
tip/tail technology: Pro-Tip (tip and tail taper at points reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
park rating: 5/10
all mountain rating: 9/10
powder rating: 7/10
shipping restriction: Only available for shipping within Australia
design inspiration: Built for biggest terrain possible, the Natural Selection competition
